<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Gangani (Ireland)</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of western Ireland recorded by Ptolemy near the Shannon estuary, sharing their name with the Gangani of north-west Wales.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150 places the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gangani-britain">Gangani</a> on the west coast of Ireland, south of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/auteini">Auteini</a> and north of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/velabri">Velabri</a>, usually located in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-clare">County Clare</a> or around the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">Shannon</a>. The same name is given to a headland in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, home of the Gangani (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>), on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llyn-peninsula">Llŷn</a> peninsula.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers or customs. The shared name on both sides of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-sea">Irish Sea</a> has been taken as evidence of migration, of an Irish group settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, or simply of a common Celtic word, perhaps connected with Irish legends of the Gamanrad, but none of these ideas can be proven.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gangani-britain">Gangani</a> of Ireland do not appear in later sources. Their region later formed part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Kingdom of Munster</a> and the lands of peoples such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ui-fidgenti">Ui Fidgenti</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gangani-ireland.jpg" alt="Gangani (Ireland)" width="320" height="352"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Rhion assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CymruLlwythi.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Ireland</dd></dl></aside></div>

